# Why this file exists.
#
# `src/renderer/src/features/audio-eq/index.ts` shipped with a raw NUL byte at
# offset 1527 (`const CUSTOM = '\0custom'`). With no .gitattributes, git guesses
# text vs binary by sniffing for a NUL in the first 8000 bytes, so it classified
# a 326-line TypeScript file as binary:
#
#   git diff  ->  "Binary files a/....ts and b/....ts differ"
#                 "src/renderer/src/features/audio-eq/index.ts | Bin 0 -> 11349 bytes"
#   git grep  ->  "Binary file src/... matches"   (no line numbers, no context)
#
# 326 lines landed unreviewable, and no reviewer could have seen the line that
# caused it. `npm run check:control-chars` now fails the build on any control
# character in tracked source; this file is the second half — even if one gets in,
# the diff stays readable, so the review that catches it is possible.
#
# `eol=lf` on top of `text` keeps the working tree LF on Windows too: a file that
# git normalises on the way in but checks out as CRLF shows every line as changed
# the first time somebody with different core.autocrlf touches it.

# THE BOOLEAN `diff` IS THE LOAD-BEARING PART, and `diff=<driver>` is NOT a
# substitute for it. Measured on this repo, on a one-line .ts file holding a NUL:
#
#   zz-probe.ts diff=typescript   ->  git diff --numstat:  -   -   zz-probe.ts
#   zz-probe.ts diff              ->  git diff --numstat:  1   0   zz-probe.ts
#
# A driver name only selects hunk-header patterns; git still autodetects binary
# and still refuses to diff. The boolean attribute is documented as "treated as
# text, even when they contain byte values that normally never appear in text
# files, such as NUL", and it is the only spelling that actually did.

* text=auto

*.ts    text eol=lf diff
*.mts   text eol=lf diff
*.cts   text eol=lf diff
*.js    text eol=lf diff
*.mjs   text eol=lf diff
*.cjs   text eol=lf diff
*.json  text eol=lf diff
*.jsonc text eol=lf diff
*.css   text eol=lf diff
*.html  text eol=lf diff
*.md    text eol=lf diff
*.yml   text eol=lf diff
*.yaml  text eol=lf diff
*.conf  text eol=lf diff
.gitattributes text eol=lf diff
.gitignore     text eol=lf diff
LICENSE        text eol=lf diff

# Genuinely binary: never diff, never normalise.
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mkv  binary
*.bdic binary
*.7z   binary
*.zip  binary
*.exe  binary
*.dll  binary
